# Nuxt.js + Vue.js + TypeScript + Telegram Bot CursorRules

description: "Architecture and code style rules for projects using Nuxt.js, Vue.js, TypeScript, and Telegram Bot moderation features."
globs: [ "*.vue", "*.ts", "*.js" ]
alwaysApply: true

## TypeScript
- Avoid `any` and `unknown` types. Always use strict typing.
- Define interfaces for API responses, Telegram events, and user-generated event models.
- Prefer type-safe enums and constants for event/action types.
- Use type inference and generics where appropriate.

## Vue.js & Nuxt.js
- Use only functional, composition API components.
- All components must implement PropTypes and emit events with strict typing.
- Use Nuxt `useHead` and `useSeoMeta` hooks for handling SEO data.
- Optimize performance: use lazy-loading (`defineAsyncComponent`), memoization, and limit prop-passing depth.
- Ensure accessibility with semantic HTML and appropriate ARIA attributes.
- Use `<NuxtImage>`, `<NuxtPicture>`, and Nuxt Icons where possible for media assets.
- Follow Vue and Nuxt file organization: `/components`, `/composables`, `/pages`, `/layouts`.

## Telegram Bot (Moderation Logic)
- All command handlers must be defined in isolated modules.
- Describe all commands, payloads, and responses with TypeScript interfaces.
- Use strong error handling: implement retry/fallback logic in all API requests.
- Validate and normalize all incoming data from users/events.
- Cover all moderation workflows with tests (unit/integration).

## HTML/CSS & Cursor
- Use `cursor: pointer` only on interactive elements (buttons, links, clickable cards).
- Use `cursor: not-allowed` for all disabled controls (inputs, buttons, custom UI).
- Use `cursor: move` for draggable interfaces (drag and drop).
- For visually custom cursors, provide appropriate fallback cursors and maintain accessibility.
- Do not override browser default cursor except for strong UX reasons.

**Note:** These CursorRules are suitable for multi-platform, type-safe, modular web applications with user-generated content and Telegram Bot API integrations. Adapt specifics as needed for your own project structure and code conventions.

